   "**The hinge is whether relief becomes a rule** — the moment exemptions are granted through a published, criteria-based process any importer can use rather than through a senator's request; the moment the two governments publish the list of measures each will remove and in what order; the moment border-state industries get a multi-year horizon instead of a pre-election window; and the moment Congress reasserts the tariff power it delegated — the chain can be broken. §2 does not forbid a markup; it insists a markup be regulated by the authority according to the value of the goods, and that the disadvantaged not be made to bear the loss."
