  "hinge": "The cause is not the virus; it is the distance between a case and a contact list. It is the choice — by Kenya's health ministry, whether the cluster is closed by a complete, paid, published tracing operation in the next fortnight or managed case by case as it appears; by the hospitals that treated the index patient before diagnosis, whether triage and isolation are rebuilt now rather than after the next undiagnosed arrival; by the WHO and the trial sponsors, whether a Bundibugyo candidate is moved at the speed of an outbreak rather than the speed of a protocol; and by the governments issuing travel advisories, whether the advisory is proportionate to eight cases. §3 does not ask for heroism; it asks for care, for healing, for consolation to those in mourning and help in all things needed — and in an outbreak that duty is measurable in tracers hired and PPE delivered this week. Whether Kenya's first outbreak ends at eight cases or becomes its first epidemic is not fixed by the species; it is a decision held by named ministers, named hospital directors and named donors, and one that a different choice could still make."
